 is the new industry standard. Every competitor reports BEAM scores. Scaling behavior is where graph memory should differentiate from flat vector stores."}]}],"id":"blk-70157","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70159","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101193","text":"Session 2: MemoryAgentBench"}]},{"id":"blk-70160","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101194","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101195","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101196","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_8889e094cb2b904d65f6a29cd7861f1c"}]}],"id":"blk-70161","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101197","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101198","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.05257"}]}],"id":"blk-70163","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101199","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repo"},{"id":"spn-101200","text":": https://github.com/HUST-AI-HYZ/MemoryAgentBench"}]}],"id":"blk-70165","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101201","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101202","text":": Multi-turn incremental format, includes EventQA and FactConsolidation"}]}],"id":"blk-70167","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101203","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101204","text":": 4 competency scores — accurate retrieval, test-time learning, long-range understanding, selective forgetting"}]}],"id":"blk-70169","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70172","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101205","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101206","text":": Multi-turn format requires simulating incremental store→query cycles, not batch ingest. Map \"selective forgetting\" to "},{"id":"spn-101207","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_by_policy"},{"id":"spn-101208","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-101209","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_node"},{"id":"spn-101210","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-70171","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101211","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101212","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101213","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memoryagentbench"}]}],"id":"blk-70173","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70176","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101214","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101215","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101216","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memoryagentbench --limit 50"}]}],"id":"blk-70175","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101217","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why second"},{"id":"spn-101218","text":": Directly tests Graphonomous's differentiating features (forgetting, learning loop). ICLR 2026 paper — high credibility."}]}],"id":"blk-70177","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70179","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101219","text":"Session 3: LMEB (Long-horizon Memory Embedding Benchmark)"}]},{"id":"blk-70180","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101220","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101221","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101222","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_81c0f91f92b9b4a52e0a38b44c49a492"}]}],"id":"blk-70181","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101223","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101224","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12572"}]}],"id":"blk-70183","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101225","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repo"},{"id":"spn-101226","text":": https://github.com/KaLM-Embedding/LMEB"}]}],"id":"blk-70185","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101227","marks":["bold"],"text":"HuggingFace"},{"id":"spn-101228","text":": https://huggingface.co/datasets/KaLM-Embedding/LMEB"}]}],"id":"blk-70187","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101229","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101230","text":": 22 datasets, 193 zero-shot retrieval tasks across 4 memory types (episodic, dialogue, semantic, procedural)"}]}],"id":"blk-70189","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101231","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101232","text":": Retrieval accuracy per memory type, aggregate score"}]}],"id":"blk-70191","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101233","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101234","text":": This benchmarks the "},{"id":"spn-101235","marks":["italic"],"text":"embedding model"},{"id":"spn-101236","text":", not the full system. Run nomic-embed-text-v2-moe through the LMEB eval harness (likely Python). May need a thin Python wrapper or direct Elixir port of the eval logic."}]}],"id":"blk-70193","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101237","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101238","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101239","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lmeb"}]}],"id":"blk-70195","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101240","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101241","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101242","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lmeb --model nomic-embed-text-v2-moe"}]}],"id":"blk-70197","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101243","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why third"},{"id":"spn-101244","text":": Cheapest to run (embedding-only, no LLM judge needed). Validates the foundational layer. If nomic scores poorly on memory-specific retrieval, that's a critical finding."}]}],"id":"blk-70199","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70201","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101245","text":"Session 4: MemoryBench (Continual Learning from Feedback)"}]},{"id":"blk-70202","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101246","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101247","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101248","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_8ef86ae124eb2f03375289107dcac5ae"}]}],"id":"blk-70203","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101249","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101250","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.17281"}]}],"id":"blk-70205","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70208","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101251","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101252","text":": User feedback simulation across multiple domains and languages"}]}],"id":"blk-70207","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101253","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101254","text":": Continual learning accuracy, feedback utilization rate, cross-domain transfer"}]}],"id":"blk-70209","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101255","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101256","text":": Requires simulating the feedback loop — "},{"id":"spn-101257","marks":["code"],"text":"learn_from_feedback"},{"id":"spn-101258","text":" with explicit/action-based/implicit feedback types, then re-querying to measure improvement. Multi-domain and multilingual means varied corpus."}]}],"id":"blk-70211","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101259","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101260","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101261","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memorybench"}]}],"id":"blk-70213","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101262","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101263","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101264","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memorybench --domain all --limit 100"}]}],"id":"blk-70215","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101265","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why fourth"},{"id":"spn-101266","text":": Directly tests the learning loop. Published finding that no system beats RAG baseline — if Graphonomous does, that's a headline result."}]}],"id":"blk-70217","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70219","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101267","text":"Session 5: LifeBench (Non-Declarative Memory)"}]},{"id":"blk-70220","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70222","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101268","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101269","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101270","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_824059ff9230ff0953646ea7ac2e7d6a"}]}],"id":"blk-70221","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101271","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101272","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.03781"}]}],"id":"blk-70223","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70226","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101273","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101274","text":": Long-horizon event simulations with real-world priors (surveys, maps, calendars)"}]}],"id":"blk-70225","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101275","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101276","text":": Accuracy on habitual/procedural memory inference, declarative vs non-declarative breakdown"}]}],"id":"blk-70227","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101277","marks":["bold"],"text":"SOTA"},{"id":"spn-101278","text":": 55.2% (top system)"}]}],"id":"blk-70229","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101279","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101280","text":": Tests "},{"id":"spn-101281","marks":["italic"],"text":"inferred"},{"id":"spn-101282","text":" knowledge, not explicitly stored facts. Graphonomous procedural nodes + edge patterns may capture habitual patterns that flat stores miss. May need to extend "},{"id":"spn-101283","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_procedural"},{"id":"spn-101284","text":" or add inference logic."}]}],"id":"blk-70231","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70234","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101285","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101286","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101287","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lifebench"}]}],"id":"blk-70233","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101288","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101289","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101290","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lifebench --limit 50"}]}],"id":"blk-70235","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101291","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why fifth"},{"id":"spn-101292","text":": Hardest benchmark (SOTA is 55%). Low expectations, high signal. If graph structure helps even marginally on non-declarative memory, that validates the architecture thesis."}]}],"id":"blk-70237","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70239","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101293","text":"Session 6: AMemGym (On-Policy Interactive)"}]},{"id":"blk-70240","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101294","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101295","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101296","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_b7ccffd9e67df8e7b42366ff24a9be82"}]}],"id":"blk-70241","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101297","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101298","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.01966"}]}],"id":"blk-70243","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101299","marks":["bold"],"text":"HuggingFace"},{"id":"spn-101300","text":": https://huggingface.co/datasets/AGI-Eval/AMemGym"}]}],"id":"blk-70245","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101301","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101302","text":": Interactive on-policy benchmark — agent generates its own conversation"}]}],"id":"blk-70247","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101303","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101304","text":": Structured state consistency, memory utilization, persona tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-70249","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101305","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101306","text":": This is fundamentally different from other benchmarks. The agent must "},{"id":"spn-101307","marks":["italic"],"text":"participate"},{"id":"spn-101308","text":" in the conversation, not just answer post-hoc questions. Requires wiring Graphonomous MCP into a simulated conversation loop with an LLM-simulated user. Most complex harness to build."}]}],"id":"blk-70251","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101309","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101310","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101311","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.amemgym"}]}],"id":"blk-70253","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101312","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101313","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101314","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.amemgym --scenarios 10"}]}],"id":"blk-70255","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101315","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why last"},{"id":"spn-101316","text":": Most complex integration. Requires LLM-in-the-loop (simulated user). But the most realistic test of how Graphonomous actually performs in production. Save for last when all other harnesses are proven."}]}],"id":"blk-70257","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70259","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101317","text":"Post-Completion"}]},{"id":"blk-70260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101318","text":"After all 6 harnesses are built and run:"}]},{"id":"blk-70261","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101319","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-101320","marks":["code"],"text":"OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"},{"id":"spn-101321","text":" with a unified results table"}]}],"id":"blk-70262","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101322","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-101323","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.com/benchmarks/"},{"id":"spn-101324","text":" pages with new benchmark results"}]}],"id":"blk-70264","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101325","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-101326","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/site/portfolio-review.html"},{"id":"spn-101327","text":" competitive landscape"}]}],"id":"blk-70266","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101328","text":"Store a comprehensive episodic node in Graphonomous summarizing the full evaluation"}]}],"id":"blk-70268","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101329","text":"Consider adding top-line scores to "},{"id":"spn-101330","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/README.md"}]}],"id":"blk-70270","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-70272","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101331","text":"Anti-Patterns to Avoid"}]},{"id":"blk-70273","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101332","text":"Do NOT modify "},{"id":"spn-101333","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-101334","text":" or the retrieval pipeline to game a specific benchmark"}]}],"id":"blk-70274","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101335","text":"Do NOT add benchmark-specific code paths to the core engine"}]}],"id":"blk-70276","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101336","text":"Do NOT skip the smoke test ("},{"id":"spn-101337","marks":["code"],"text":"--limit 50"},{"id":"spn-101338","text":") before full runs"}]}],"id":"blk-70278","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101339","text":"Do NOT fabricate competitive baselines — only cite published numbers with sources"}]}],"id":"blk-70280","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101340","text":"Do NOT skip storing results in Graphonomous — the learning loop is the point"}]}],"id":"blk-70282","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraqee4yjmvsm2lvmslnyvpxev4gsmfamzb2lhlsffnb5gmjnl24yva","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}